{
  "_description": "Google Gemini CLI auto-approve permissions for safe, read-only operations. Merged into ~/.gemini/settings.json during installation. See trusted-domains.json for the domain allowlist.",

  "_hardening": {
    "_note": "v3.17.0 Phase 1.1 rescoped this baseline to be read-only at the side-effect level. Gemini matches by PREFIX, so a bare entry such as run_shell_command(find) admitted 'find . -delete'. Unlike Claude Code there is no built-in read-only command set to fall back on, so removals here are a genuine coverage reduction and were limited to entries that are mutation-capable regardless of redirection. Full matcher evidence in docs/releases/v3/v3.17/development/permission-matcher-findings.md.",
    "_reference_pattern": "run_shell_command(sed -n) - admits the read-only -n form while excluding sed -i.",
    "removed_v3_17_0": {
      "find": "Prefix match admits -delete, -exec, -fprintf and -execdir.",
      "sort": "Prefix match admits sort -o FILE, which writes. No prefix can express 'sort without -o'.",
      "awk": "An awk program can write via BEGIN{print > \"/path\"}; program text is arbitrary.",
      "gh api": "Admits --method POST|PATCH|PUT|DELETE. The specific gh read entries retain the useful coverage.",
      "git branch, git tag, git remote": "Admit -D, -d and add/remove/set-url respectively. Replaced by read-only subcommand prefixes.",
      "ip, sysctl, ss, journalctl, dmesg": "Admit ip link set, sysctl -w, ss -K, journalctl --vacuum-*, dmesg -C. Replaced by pinned read forms.",
      "xcrun, xcode-select": "xcrun executes an arbitrary named tool; xcode-select --switch mutates the active toolchain. Replaced by query forms.",
      "env": "Prefix match admits 'env FOO=bar rm -rf /', because env runs an arbitrary inner command. Claude's Bash(env) is an EXACT match and stays, which is precisely the prefix-versus-glob asymmetry this file's matcher note describes. printenv is retained as the read-only equivalent."
    },
    "known_gaps": {
      "separator_splitting": "Whether Gemini's matcher splits a compound command on &&, ; or | the way Claude Code's does is UNVERIFIED. If it does not, any prefix entry is reachable via chaining. Tracked for Phase 6.2.",
      "windows_shell_coverage": "This file ships no PowerShell or cmd.exe set, so a Windows Gemini user receives a POSIX-shaped allowlist. Deliberately not expanded in Phase 1.1 (rescope only); handed to sub-task 5.3 for documentation."
    }
  },

